{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/114683-classic-world-of-darkness-and-the-year-2014","id":114683,"title":"Classic World of Darkness and the year 2014","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-17T06:27:05-07:00","id":114683,"title":"Classic World of Darkness and the year 2014","content":"I know theres a 20 Years of Mage/Werewolf/Vampire/Wraith/Blahblahblahblahsomethingsomethingworldofdarkness The Electric Boogalo edition. but which concepts have you add to your game(that are current and modern) and how has this changed your experience as a DM?<br /> <br /> as for my Mage game, ill say it. Hispter Hollow Ones that use starbucks as Nodes. Its so stupidly hilarious seeing this guys trying to pull coincidencial magic as both stuff from scott pilgrim and trying to &quot;Keep it Under&quot; because &quot;Oh, you woudnt get it.&quot;<br /> <br /> as for hunter. i loved the idea of the Network Zero from H:tV and im using a lot of the social media, youtube, instagram etc... on my settings for Hunters to use as guides of what they might be facing.<br /> <br /> Wraith: oh man....I had to, im sorry but i had too. im keeping as a running gag a little chronicle here and there where &quot;A group of experts on the supernatural are send into a house to investigate occult phenomena. They are known as The GhostFacers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Im interested in maybe picking up changeling and for what i seen, i been thinking of making some of my changelings to pass around as &quot;Cosplayers.&quot; (due to their clothings and such)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T09:38:04-07:00","id":114749,"title":"","content":"I've been running urban changelings as hipsters and members of maker communities - the sorts 20/30 somethings trying to reclaim urban decay and make it their own. Those sorts of groups are great for accepting Kithain eccentricities and being fertile ground for inspiration and glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T10:35:32-07:00","id":114794,"title":"","content":"well in my game Tehnomancy for the Tremere is no longer very secret much unique wow so underground. Most big cities have at least one Tremere with a few point in it (among neonates is about as common as movement of the mind or lure of the flame)<br /> <br /> maybe other thigns to but i cant think of many right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T02:54:39-07:00","id":115184,"title":"","content":"The biggest change I've made has been in my mage games. I run that starting in the early 2000s, the Technocratic paradigm started breaking down. The technocratic paradigm is entirely based on the idea of science logically explaining how and why something unexplainable is happening, which in the 90s and earlier was a big thing. But really since the 2000s, the population's mentality has shifted. It's all about convenience again. People don't WANT to know how their computer works, they just want it to work. If it breaks, they don't read the manual and try to figure out how to fix it. They try a couple of half-baked basically arcane rituals (turn it off and turn it on again as the solution to everything), or they send it in to the company to &quot;just fix it&quot;. In short, the idea of explaining something logically is no longer the protection from paradox that it once was because that isn't the sort of explanation consensus reality is looking for anymore. Consensus has gotten really good at ignoring facts and more and more insists on ignoring them in favor of their original assumption. This is death for the technocratic paradigm. In response to this I run a much more even footing in the Ascension War with the Progenitors and Iteration X leaving the Technocratic Union and joining the Traditions as they could no longer justify to themselves that what they were doing wasn't magic as more and more of them kept getting hit with paradox for things that had made perfectly logical sense to them, and the Void Engineers just going off into the aether and vanishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T20:41:14-07:00","id":117819,"title":"","content":"Wraith and Demon. Consider the Sixth Great Maelstrom never happened (as a necessary condition for a Wraith chronicle set after 1999). It also means the storm never cracked the walls of the Abyss (so, no Demon the Fallen). The only compromise I could work out between the two game lines is assuming the Sixth Great Maelstrom affected the Underworld as much as the preceding five (with the difference it was not triggered by anything happening this side of the Shroud). <br /> <br /> Now, with all that in mind, consider DtF's particular plot, culminating with Lucifer's visage in LA. It would make the WoD a far more superstitious place. Of course, many wouldn't believe it was a angel or a demon, and many would try to find a rational explanation. However, many would, at least temporarily, renew their faith, and considering the WoD, I don't know how good it would be. I'd say a general atmosphere of superstition and obscurantism covers the world, specially the U.S. Also, all the scientific truths are shattered by Lucifer's Revelation, and the resulting insecurity impacts the cultural zeitgeist.<br /> <br /> If Hurricane Katrina impacted America's psyche, a &quot;natural&quot; tragedy such as the Devil's Night earthquake would impact it on a deeper level. The world suddenly becomes a even more hostile place, and most start wondering what other catastrophes await in the future? Guess people in the WoD would respond to that by adopting a even more inconsequential attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T13:21:07-07:00","id":118076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/114683-classic-world-of-darkness-and-the-year-2014?p=117819#post117819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith and Demon. Consider the Sixth Great Maelstrom never happened (as a necessary condition for a Wraith chronicle set after 1999). It also means the storm never cracked the walls of the Abyss (so, no Demon the Fallen). The only compromise I could work out between the two game lines is assuming the Sixth Great Maelstrom affected the Underworld as much as the preceding five (with the difference it was not triggered by anything happening this side of the Shroud).<br /> <br /> Now, with all that in mind, consider DtF's particular plot, culminating with Lucifer's visage in LA. It would make the WoD a far more superstitious place. Of course, many wouldn't believe it was a angel or a demon, and many would try to find a rational explanation. However, many would, at least temporarily, renew their faith, and considering the WoD, I don't know how good it would be. I'd say a general atmosphere of superstition and obscurantism covers the world, specially the U.S. Also, all the scientific truths are shattered by Lucifer's Revelation, and the resulting insecurity impacts the cultural zeitgeist.<br /> <br /> If Hurricane Katrina impacted America's psyche, a &quot;natural&quot; tragedy such as the Devil's Night earthquake would impact it on a deeper level. The world suddenly becomes a even more hostile place, and most start wondering what other catastrophes await in the future? Guess people in the WoD would respond to that by adopting a even more inconsequential attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying the Sixth Great Maelstrom never happened is not &quot;a necessary condition for a Wraith chronicle set after 1999&quot;. There's a very simple hack that has worked quite well for us. Just treat the Sixth Great Maelstroms as exactly like all the other Maelstroms and even the previous 5 Great Maelstroms that have occurred. Eventually it died down. I usually run the Underworld as an absolute wreck, saying that the Sixth Great Maelstrom didn't completely die down until 2003 (the release of Demon the Fallen) but that it didn't rage forever. This is necessary, not just for Wraith, but for any vampire chronicle in Revised as well (or the Giovanni really have nothing do do anymore). What has worked well in addition is to say that in most places, the Shroud is still the Shroud, but that in other places due to the unpredictable power of the Storm it did harden into the Stormwall, thus allowing Orpheus to exist as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T18:44:53-07:00","id":118202,"title":"","content":"Both Mummy: the Resurrection and Hunter: the Reckoning also require the 6GM as part of their origins. In fact MtR's backstory directly involves itself in the events that sparked the 6GM. In fact only Orpheus doesn't actually require the 6GM to exist.<br /> <br /> But Orpheus does have a lot of interesting WtO related material and I would highly recommend it if you're looking for Wraith stuff in a post-6GM world. Plus it's a great and terribly under appreciated game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T21:37:42-07:00","id":118252,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I got reminded of one other important change I do make. Mummy the Resurrection never happened. I cannot stress how much I hate that storyline. I loved 2nd edition Mummy and Revised completely ruined all their flavor and made them half-changelings with a slightly egyptian feel. They're not the same thing any more, not to mention that using that storyline completely shits all over both the Silent Striders metaplot in werewolf and blows up the Children of Osiris in vampire. And on top of all of that, it accomplishes this by finding the True Spell of Life? It's an incredibly contrived plot line that ruins one entire sphere that actually worked fantastically in cross-sphere, shits on two others, and adds an unnecessary carbon copy that doesn't even fit with the other WoD spheres at all.<br /> <br /> End Rant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T00:14:30-07:00","id":118301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/114683-classic-world-of-darkness-and-the-year-2014?p=118076#post118076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying the Sixth Great Maelstrom never happened is not &quot;a necessary condition for a Wraith chronicle set after 1999&quot;. There's a very simple hack that has worked quite well for us. Just treat the Sixth Great Maelstroms as exactly like all the other Maelstroms and even the previous 5 Great Maelstroms that have occurred. Eventually it died down. I usually run the Underworld as an absolute wreck, saying that the Sixth Great Maelstrom didn't completely die down until 2003 (the release of Demon the Fallen) but that it didn't rage forever. This is necessary, not just for Wraith, but for any vampire chronicle in Revised as well (or the Giovanni really have nothing do do anymore). What has worked well in addition is to say that in most places, the Shroud is still the Shroud, but that in other places due to the unpredictable power of the Storm it did harden into the Stormwall, thus allowing Orpheus to exist as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said: the Sixth Great Maelstrom happened, but it didn't resulted in the end of WtO (it was just another Maelstrom). It cracked the gates to the Abyss, however (thus allowing DtF).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T02:46:35-07:00","id":118350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/114683-classic-world-of-darkness-and-the-year-2014?p=118301#post118301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I said: the Sixth Great Maelstrom happened, but it didn't resulted in the end of WtO (it was just another Maelstrom). It cracked the gates to the Abyss, however (thus allowing DtF).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Exactly. It was not intended to contradict your statement. I was noting that so many seem to think the only way to play WoD anymore is to remove all of the metaplot from Revised entirely. I was agreeing with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}